//RS             | "DataErrorKind"
//RS             | "DurationUnit"
//RS             | "LocalDate"
//RS             // D-RANGE-VALUE1=A puts Range in auto_equatable, so sema rewrites
//RS             // `a == b` on two Ranges into the Equatable.equal method shape. Every
//RS             // other link already exists: lowering turns an admitted `.equal` into
//RS             // TExprKind::Binary{Eq}, the interpreter evaluates that node for a
